    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Jackson Merrill**, whose 75.26 score makes him our most potent asset. His matchup against L\u00f3pez is bolstered by an 85% stolen base success rate against the pitcher\u2019s delivery, providing an elite environment for his speed-oriented profile. Joining him at the top of the priority list is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), who benefits significantly from a favorable clash with Lorenzen. The combination of Lorenzen\u2019s 4.82 xERA, park-adjusted hitting conditions, and a strong order slot creates a perfect storm for production. **Nasim Nunez** (68.96) also warrants attention; despite hitting lower in the order, his utility value is inflated by the same favorable conditions and the switch-hitting versatility he offers against the opposing staff.\n\nWhile the core is robust, several tactical decisions define today's roster. We are closely monitoring the matchup for **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker**, both of whom face a significant hurdle in Wheeler. Despite their strong skill sets, the elite nature of the opposing arm\u2014combined with a catcher adept at suppressing the run game\u2014drags their efficiency scores down, particularly for **Andy Pages** (50.49). The most difficult decision involved **Miguel Vargas**, who was narrowly excluded from the starting nine. Although his xwOBA of .399 is impressive, his projected efficiency (56.16) fell just short of our target for a high-volume start, as the optimizer prioritized the platoon-neutral power of players like **Josh Jung** and the table-setting upside of **Drake Baldwin**. \n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding the slate's volatility. The most significant blow is the confirmed rainout of **Gunnar Henderson**, which effectively removes our anchor from consideration and necessitates this pivot to our depth chart. Furthermore, while we expect a strong day from our speedsters, **Heliot Ramos** faces a minor headwind against a pitcher who excels at holding runners, curbing his base-stealing upside even if his hitting projection remains sound. We will look to **Curtis Mead** and **Brayan Rocchio** to provide stability as they look to exploit their respective platoon advantages against soft-tossing opponents.",
